Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: allow framebuffers below 64x64 on MT8183

mtk_drm_kms_init() defaults mode_config.min_width/min_height to 64
unless the SoC data sets them; MT8188/MT8195 set 1, MT8183 did not.
On Krane the status bar buffer is 42x1920 in panel orientation, so
AddFB2 failed with -EINVAL ("bad framebuffer width 42"),
drm_hwcomposer could not put the layer on a plane, and because its
client range has to be contiguous the full-screen launcher between
the scaled wallpaper and the status bar was GPU-composited as well
(91% of the pixel work while scrolling the home screen).

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
@@ -278,6 +278,13 @@
 	.ext_path = mt8183_mtk_ddp_ext,
 	.ext_len = ARRAY_SIZE(mt8183_mtk_ddp_ext),
 	.mmsys_dev_num = 1,
+	/*
+	 * The OVL layers take any size. The 64x64 default rejected the
+	 * 42 px wide Android status bar in AddFB2, so it and every layer
+	 * between it and the wallpaper went to GPU composition.
+	 */
+	.min_width = 1,
+	.min_height = 1,
 };
 
 static const struct mtk_mmsys_driver_data mt8186_mmsys_driver_data = {
